  "notes": "Boards lie FLAT ON the tube faces, coplanar with them, and reach out sideways past the tube edge -- tangentially, not radially (confirmed from the bench, hall_probe_setup_2.png). The four arms on a ring therefore form a pinwheel. Because the board lies flat, its 30 mm foot runs along the tube, which is what sets the 33 mm plate pitch (30 mm plate + ~3 mm gap), 4 to a face. Tube is 1 inch (25.4 mm) outside width. Arm dimensions from the SENIS eval-kit drawing: 92 mm PCB, FSV 3 mm from the tip, 0.55 mm above the board, board 1.2 mm thick -- so each chip sits 1.75 mm off its face and reaches 76.3 mm across it. STILL UNVERIFIED: arm_sense (which way round the tube the arms point), the sensor-to-face mapping below, and each chip_rot_deg / axis_signs. Only the 3D arrangement and the tube-frame rotation depend on those -- |B|, the channel health diagnostics and the raw exports do not. Establish the real order with octobee_idmap.py and a slow magnet pass along one face, correct the entries, then press Reload geometry in the GUI.",
